WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:14.735
Zann thought in surprise.

2
00:00:15.295 --> 00:00:17.396
"We never told Vilkor anything about Magica.

3
00:00:18.016 --> 00:00:19.337
How did he come up with that name?

4
00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:20.777
Did Mellis tell him?"

5
00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:25.838
Perda let out a gasp so loud that a man glanced over in surprise.

6
00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.399
"Oh, wow!"

7
00:00:27.899 --> 00:00:28.639
she blurted out.

8
00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:31.180
Then she grabbed Zann by the arm.

9
00:00:31.756 --> 00:00:32.276
"Come with me.

10
00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:33.197
We have to talk!"

11
00:00:33.937 --> 00:00:38.539
Feeling confused, Zann allowed Perda to drag him away and into the woods.

12
00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:40.360
Zing hurried after them.

13
00:00:42.961 --> 00:00:46.702
When Perda turned to face Zann, she looked pale and stunned.

14
00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:47.863
"What is it?"

15
00:00:48.243 --> 00:00:48.683
he asked.

16
00:00:48.703 --> 00:00:49.824
"Are you okay?"

17
00:00:49.844 --> 00:00:51.504
"Don't you get it?"

18
00:00:51.924 --> 00:00:52.405
she asked.

19
00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:53.745
"Get what?"

20
00:00:54.445 --> 00:00:55.686
Zann scratched his head.

21
00:00:55.706 --> 00:00:57.947
"Are you talking about what Vilkor just said?"

22
00:00:58.847 --> 00:01:00.148
"Yes!" Perda said.

23
00:01:00.576 --> 00:01:05.501
"It explains everything—like why the stars and trees and other stuff seem so familiar.

24
00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:09.384
And why the rock trompers look similar to trolls.

25
00:01:10.045 --> 00:01:13.668
And why the worlds we visited the other day seemed so odd."

26
00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:17.531
Zann tapped his chin, barely paying attention.

27
00:01:17.551 --> 00:01:20.514
"I wonder if Zira overheard us talking about Magica.

28
00:01:21.054 --> 00:01:23.777
She spied on us a lot to learn about magic, remember?

29
00:01:24.658 --> 00:01:27.872
Maybe she heard us mention the name of our world to Mellis."

30
00:01:27.892 --> 00:01:30.794
Perda grabbed him by the shoulders, staring into his eyes.

31
00:01:30.814 --> 00:01:33.295
"This is our land.

32
00:01:33.836 --> 00:01:36.597
Terrica is Magica!"

33
00:01:37.398 --> 00:01:40.479
Zann was a little distracted by Perda's pretty brown eyes.

34
00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:44.582
"Huh?" he said, trying to focus on what she was saying.

35
00:01:44.602 --> 00:01:47.924
"Yeah, I know, Vilkor decided to rename it.

36
00:01:48.244 --> 00:01:51.005
But how did he—" "You're not listening to me!"

37
00:01:51.746 --> 00:01:55.328
Perda let go of Zann's shoulders and started pacing back and forth.

38
00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.790
"Don't you see what's happening yet?

39
00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.812
Even that riddle should have given us a clue.

40
00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:09.359
Remember?" She stopped, cleared her throat, and quoted the verse from Zann's parents' lab: "Bygone days lost to

41
00:02:09.439 --> 00:02:18.506
time's haze Yet visible to careful gaze Rooted in the depths of time Touch and see—no need to

42
00:02:18.587 --> 00:02:23.711
climb." Zann was impressed that Perda remembered the rhyme so perfectly.

43
00:02:24.371 --> 00:02:25.092
Then he blinked.

44
00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.963
"Wait," he said slowly, finally catching on.

45
00:02:28.983 --> 00:02:30.324
"'Bygone days.'

46
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:33.927
Do you mean "Yes, Zann," Perda said.

47
00:02:33.947 --> 00:02:41.114
"When we fell into that strange wormhole at the base of the Wormwood tree, we didn't travel to

48
00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:41.934
another world.

49
00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.737
We traveled back in time!"

50
00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:49.181
Zann gasped, hardly daring to believe it was true.

51
00:02:49.761 --> 00:02:52.724
But the more he thought about it, the more sense it made to him.

52
00:02:53.804 --> 00:02:55.965
"The swamps near the mines," he blurted out.

53
00:02:55.985 --> 00:02:58.985
"I thought the birdcalls there sounded familiar!"

54
00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.246
Perda nodded.

55
00:03:00.266 --> 00:03:05.287
"You must have been in the place that will be Swamp Bottom someday."

56
00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:08.448
Just then there was a rustle in the bushes nearby.

57
00:03:09.128 --> 00:03:13.289
A chupo poked its snout out, sniffed at the kids, and then howled.

58
00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.871
Zing chirped in alarm, and then shot a stream of flames at the chupo.

59
00:03:17.891 --> 00:03:22.792
"Good boy," Zann said to the dragon as the chupo disappeared.

60
00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.981
"Let's get away from here," Perda said.

61
00:03:26.001 --> 00:03:28.842
"Someone might come to investigate that howl."

62
00:03:29.763 --> 00:03:31.283
They headed deeper into the woods.

63
00:03:31.964 --> 00:03:34.705
It was dark beneath the canopy of twisted trees.

64
00:03:35.425 --> 00:03:40.828
Noisy insects buzzed in the air, and Zann could hear animals moving just out of sight.

65
00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.630
"It's creepy in here," he said with a shudder.

66
00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.891
"Maybe this is Mount Mystery!

67
00:03:47.551 --> 00:03:49.452
That would explain why it's so scary."

68
00:03:50.444 --> 00:03:54.347
He searched his mind, trying to remember what he'd learned in history class.

69
00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.588
"Do you think this is the Old Times?"

70
00:03:57.809 --> 00:03:58.369
"I doubt it."

71
00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.050
Perda looked thoughtful.

72
00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:06.675
"In the Old Times, there was a ton of dark magic, and everyone used all kinds of dangerous

73
00:04:06.715 --> 00:04:10.758
spells. No, I think this is the time before that."

74
00:04:10.778 --> 00:04:12.999
"Before the Old Times?

75
00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.101
Wow." Zann tried to imagine it.

76
00:04:16.621 --> 00:04:20.224
Then he realized he didn't have to imagine it—he was living it!

77
00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.702
"Right," Perda went on, sounding awed.

78
00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:29.708
"We're in the distant past, and that scrawny little tree near the well must be the Wormwood tree.

79
00:04:30.408 --> 00:04:34.251
We witnessed Mellis opening the Source of magic!"

80
00:04:35.292 --> 00:04:39.776
Zann thought hard as he trudged through the forest with Zing flying overhead.

81
00:04:39.796 --> 00:04:42.959
"The wormhole by the tree," he said.

82
00:04:42.979 --> 00:04:45.901
"It brought us to a vortex through time, right?

83
00:04:46.462 --> 00:04:52.621
So then when we went through the other wormhole "It took us into the regular vortex," Perda said,

84
00:04:52.922 --> 00:04:53.902
finishing his sentence.

85
00:04:53.922 --> 00:05:00.625
"And since we're in the distant past here, we're also in the distant past in all the other

86
00:05:00.705 --> 00:05:01.765
worlds we visited."

87
00:05:01.785 --> 00:05:05.527
"So that really was Skellia that we visited," Zann said.

88
00:05:05.547 --> 00:05:08.208
"It just hasn't been covered in water yet."

89
00:05:08.228 --> 00:05:13.730
"And the Niffians haven't yet built their beautiful towns," Perda said.

90
00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:18.112
"It's also why nobody in Wyssa's home world had heard of her.

91
00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:21.826
She won't be born until years and years from now!"

92
00:05:21.846 --> 00:05:24.788
"Let's circle back toward the village," Zann said.

93
00:05:24.808 --> 00:05:27.090
"We have to tell Mellis about this."

94
00:05:28.771 --> 00:05:32.074
They reached the clearing just in time to hear Mellis speaking.

95
00:05:32.094 --> 00:05:35.056
"It's not difficult at all!"

96
00:05:35.496 --> 00:05:37.297
she said, her voice shaking a little.

97
00:05:37.318 --> 00:05:41.921
"If you just rub your hands together—" "Silence!"

98
00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:46.024
Vilkor roared, striding over and grabbing her by the shoulder.

99
00:05:46.624 --> 00:05:50.467
He covered her mouth with his free hand and then shouted, "Zap!"

100
00:05:51.488 --> 00:05:55.171
The two of them disappeared to cries of confusion from the villagers.

101
00:05:55.692 --> 00:05:58.094
Vilkor's servants and goons seemed alarmed.

102
00:05:58.114 --> 00:06:00.976
"Hey, where'd they go?"

103
00:06:01.557 --> 00:06:02.237
a goon said.

104
00:06:02.818 --> 00:06:04.479
The clearing erupted into chaos.

105
00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.883
Servants, goons, and villagers started running around, shouting in alarm.

106
00:06:08.903 --> 00:06:15.460
"I bet Vilkor zapped them back to the village," Perda said to Zann.

107
00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:20.502
"Zira probably did that Muting spell on Mellis, and he doesn't know how to restore it."

108
00:06:21.422 --> 00:06:24.523
Zann nodded, grabbing Zing and taking Perda's arm.

109
00:06:24.543 --> 00:06:26.924
"We have to get back there and save her!"

110
00:06:27.304 --> 00:06:27.744
he cried.

111
00:06:28.365 --> 00:06:32.826
He gulped, glancing up at the peak of what he now knew was Mount Mystery.

112
00:06:32.846 --> 00:06:36.247
"And then figure out what we're going to do about all this!"
